{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Operator-authorised `systemctl restart docker` executed 2026-09-05 05:23 UTC — the BuildKit cap is now genuinely IN EFFECT, which was this ticket's AC4 dependency on epic 6202's caps.\n\n## Verified, not assumed\n\n```\nbuilder.gc in /etc/docker/daemon.json = {\"enabled\": true, \"maxUsedSpace\": \"5368709120\"}   (5 GiB)\ndaemon.json written:              2026-09-05 01:01:06 UTC\ndockerd ActiveEnterTimestamp:     2026-09-05 05:23:33 UTC   <- started AFTER the policy\n```\n\nThat ordering is the whole point. `builder.gc` is read only at daemon START — a SIGHUP reload exits 0 without applying it, which is why S2's cap script deliberately refuses to auto-restart and instead reports INSTALLED-but-NOT-IN-EFFECT until an operator schedules one. It had been in that state since 01:01.\n\n## Immediate effect, measured across the restart\n\n```\n              before                          after\nBuild Cache   6.108GB total, 15 ACTIVE        5.347GB total, 0 ACTIVE\nImages        3.079GB, 957.3MB reclaimable    3.33GB, 1.129GB reclaimable\n```\n\nRoot filesystem 37G used of 60G (61%). The `rebar-docker-buildkit-cache-high` alarm should clear as the GC prunes toward the 5 GiB share; the next probe tick will tell.\n\n## Window selection, recorded because it was the constraint all night\n\nThe restart was deferred repeatedly and deliberately: it takes Gerrit, the review-bot, the opcert service and the MCP down together, and doing it during in-flight CI costs spurious `Verified -1`s on an already-saturated queue. It ran only once all of these held simultaneously — load average 2.72 (against 8.08 earlier), `rebar-autodeploy.service` INACTIVE, and the review bot having emitted `voter_voted` one second before the check, i.e. idle rather than mid-review.\n\nRecovery confirmed: all four containers healthy within ~20 s, Gerrit `GET /` returning HTTP 200.\n\nNote this does NOT complete this ticket's dependency by itself — S4 (`2ba3`, /var/tmp) is in review as change 2659 and S5 (`910b`) is still open, so the bounded ceiling AC4 names is not yet whole."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788585940214319001,"uuid":"45bb4e11-fb17-4c7d-ab26-87121e3eef31"}